guamp: GPU time of every user job from CP_ALWAYS_ON_COUNTER samples (after the prologue, after the IBs) and hooks for the board frame accounting (guamp-gpu-perf, default off)

With native_adreno_perf_ts set (GuampGpuPerf.inc), an A6XX framed submission copies CP_ALWAYS_ON_COUNTER (19.2 MHz) to the fence
page at 0x800 + 16 * (fence & 63) with CP_REG_TO_MEM, as a6xx_submit() fills rbmemptrs_stats alwayson_start/end; the end sample
follows a CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE while the prologue has one. native_adreno_perf_begin/end are called at a job s submission and release,
native_adreno_perf_mark gets the frame report markers 0x2000..0x3fff (adreno-metal 0023). All off: no ring word, no call.

